{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4596902","formula":"C₁₄H₁₁N","hill":"C14H11N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":11.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"6-methyl-2-(phenylethynyl)pyridine"},"descriptions":{"en":"2-Methyl-6-(phenylethynyl)pyridine (MPEP) is a research drug which was one of the first compounds found to act as a selective antagonist for the metabotropic glutamate receptor subtype mGluR5. After being originally patented as a liquid crystal for LCDs, it was developed by the pharmaceutical company Novartis in the late 1990s. It was found to produce neuroprotective effects following acute brain injury in animal studies, although it was unclear whether these results were purely from mGluR5 blockade as it also acts as a weak NMDA antagonist, and as a positive allosteric modulator of another subtype mGluR4, and there is also evidence for a functional interaction between mGluR5 and NMDA recept…"},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":3025961,"mass":193.24,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=NC(=CC=C1)C#CC2=CC=CC=C2","inchikey":"NEWKHUASLBMWRE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-methyl-6-(2-phenylethynyl)pyridine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3025961","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.384,"y":0.839,"z":0.144,"el":"N"},{"x":3.734,"y":0.774,"z":0.133,"el":"C"},{"x":1.73,"y":-0.326,"z":-0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":4.453,"y":-0.393,"z":-0.065,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.32,"y":-0.02,"z":-0.004,"el":"C"},{"x":2.351,"y":-1.544,"z":-0.261,"el":"C"},{"x":3.741,"y":-1.57,"z":-0.265,"el":"C"},{"x":4.466,"y":2.056,"z":0.351,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.999,"y":0.434,"z":-1.135,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.032,"y":-0.369,"z":1.143,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.39,"y":0.539,"z":-1.118,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.423,"y":-0.265,"z":1.16,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.102,"y":0.19,"z":0.029,"el":"C"},{"x":0.304,"y":-0.218,"z":-0.036,"el":"C"},{"x":-0